sequenceDiagram
    %% Inbound PRIVMSG: filter, persist, fan out, then async URL preview.
    autonumber
    participant Srv as IRC server
    participant H as irc.handler (handler_messages.go)
    participant Ign as ignore list (control.db)
    participant Ctl as control.db (buffer_registry)
    participant Log as network log DB
    participant NS as netsplitTracker
    participant Hub as hub.Hub
    participant WS as api/ws.go writer
    participant C as Client
    participant PQ as preview queue
    participant F as preview.Fetcher
    participant PDB as previews.db
    participant Web as remote page

    Srv->>H: PRIVMSG #chan :text https://example.com
    H->>H: ensureUTF8(content), extract msgid/account tags
    H->>Ign: ignoreLevel(sender)
    alt level = hide
        H-->>Srv: dropped, nothing stored
    else level = mute
        H->>H: muted = true (stored and shown, never counts unread)
    end
    H->>Ctl: ensureBuffer(name, kind) -> global buffer id
    opt buffer is an archived query
        H->>Ctl: syncBufferArchived(false)
        H->>Hub: Publish BufferUpdateEvent{archived: false}
        Note over Ctl: New activity resurfaces an archived DM (IRCCloud behavior).
    end
    H->>Log: InsertLogMessage(bufferID, msgid, ts, sender, kind, content, raw)
    Note over Log: UUIDv7 id (byte order == time order).<br/>FTS5 triggers index content+sender.<br/>Duplicate (buffer_id, msgid) is a no-op insert.
    Log-->>H: id, storedTS, inserted
    alt not inserted (duplicate msgid)
        H-->>Srv: no event published
    end
    opt channel quit/join
        H->>NS: trackNetsplit(...)
        NS-->>H: NetsplitMeta or nil
        opt cluster just reached NetsplitMinQuits
            NS->>Hub: Publish NetsplitEvent{message_ids} (retroactive patch)
        end
    end
    H->>H: WithSemantics(nick) - display_kind, is_self, mentions_me,<br/>counts_as_unread, highlight, sender_color, mIRC segments
    H->>Hub: Publish MessageEvent
    Hub->>WS: fan-out to every subscriber (256-buffer chan)
    Note over Hub,WS: Full buffer drops the event and closes the<br/>overflow chan. The socket tears down and the<br/>client resyncs from GET /api/state.
    WS->>C: JSON frame {"type":"message",...}

    H->>PQ: Enqueue(networkID, bufferID, messageID, content)
    Note over PQ: 256-slot buffered chan - a full queue logs and drops.
    PQ->>F: worker picks job, ExtractURLs(content)
    F->>PDB: Get(url, CacheTTL)
    alt cache miss
        F->>Web: HEAD then GET (SSRF guard, size + timeout capped)
        Web-->>F: OpenGraph / oEmbed / content-type
        F->>PDB: Put(URLPreview)
    end
    F->>Log: InsertMessagePreviewLinks(message_id, url, position)
    F->>Hub: Publish preview.Event{previews} (displayable only)
    Hub->>WS: fan-out
    WS->>C: JSON frame {"type":"preview",...}
